From 48fb91505c22ad330edaa0549f817db4fbedbcca Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: webby <webby@localhost>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 22:04:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] WC compositor: show video frames without waiting for the main
 thread

A decoded frame used to reach the screen through the page: the streaming thread
handed it to the main thread and waited, the main thread flushed the layer in
its next rendering update, and that update went to the GPU process. A page that
keeps its main thread busy (YouTube does) delayed and dropped frames that had
been decoded in time, and every frame was a few milliseconds late or early
depending on where the main thread was.

Once the compositor has the video's layer and has been shown a shared texture
in it, the graphics layer gives the platform layer a presenter: an object that
sends RemoteWCLayerTreeHost::PresentSharedTexture straight to the GPU process
and may be used on any thread. The player calls it on the streaming thread,
right after copying the frame, and no longer waits for the main thread. The
GPU process shows the texture in the layer and paints the scene again as the
last update left it.
